  "limitations": [
    "Specific mapped Banteay Samré: low laterite outer enclosure and four open gates; inner sandstone gallery with true open passages and window recesses; tall stepped lotus-bud sanctuary on a moulded plinth, eastern mandapa and two separately based libraries, corbelled roofs, original simplified pediment rims and stairs. Inner courts retain native ground. Heights, unmapped hall/library placement, surviving roof details and exact carving are picture-led approximations.",
    "Exact-QID relation3045426 and standard native multipolygon52776561178674 preserve an84x82m outer enclosure,43m inner gallery with real courtyard hole and10x9m central sanctuary control. Native east/south at heading0, internal architectural angle-0.100314380462rad. Outer gate positions follow mapped courtyard notches; inner axial passages follow gallery jogs. Eastern mandapa, paired library positions, roof subdivisions and secondary thresholds inside the courtyard are picture-led approximations rather than separately mapped building surveys.",
